{"diagnosis": "Loopback UART failed with TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0xfc want 0xa5 and tohost FAIL 0xdead via simpleuart instance at picosoc/picosoc.v:190 of module at picosoc/simpleuart.v:20. TX shifter at excerpt line 131 uses {1'b1, send_pattern[9:2]} which drops bit[1] each baud tick and mis-sizes the 10-bit frame loaded at line 126, corrupting ser_tx. Correct right-shift with idle-1 fill is {1'b1, send_pattern[9:1]} to preserve start/data/stop bits.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -130,4 +130,4 @@
 			if (send_divcnt > cfg_divider && send_bitcnt) begin
-				send_pattern <= {1'b1, send_pattern[9:2]};
+				send_pattern <= {1'b1, send_pattern[9:1]};
 				send_bitcnt <= send_bitcnt - 1;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
", "expected": "tohost PASS, TRAP cleared, uart loopback 0xa5 matches"}

